er a console.warn; and :224-225 DISCARDS that return value, so indexSession reports success and no job row, session field or ledger records the loss. FILED ISS-116 (high). Full ceremony despite not being a security finding, per this repo's own severity gate: it is a data-write path, and the gate says data writes get ceremony "regardless of severity". No round-cap concern - this is the FIRST live exercise of the U1.3 seam; every prior PASS on it was measured against fixtures. NO UNIT OVERCLAIMED, and I looked for it specifically. qa/manifests/embed-on-index.md states in its own evidence block "No live row has been written... C8 should stay open until a live run", and its checker held C8 open rather than crediting intent. U1.1/U1.2/U1.3 each PASSed on what they actually evidenced - fixture-level behaviour, mutation-proven degrade-safety, nine attack shapes leaving `chunks` untouched. What the three PASSes could not see is the one thing only a live run shows, and the moment a live run happened it showed it. That is the deferral working, not a defect in the deferral. ISS-113 UPDATED IN PLACE rather than duplicated: its title and evidence now record (b)/(c) discharged and (a) failing, superseding an outage premise that is stale. It stays `open` on (a) alone. ISS-114 COLLIDED DURING THIS SWEEP - live corroboration of an open gate. I read max(id)=113, wrote ISS-114, and found the lane/a-speakers loop had committed its own ISS-114 and ISS-115 in the interval. Renumbered mine to ISS-116; ledger re-validated at 116 rows, 0 parse errors, 0 duplicate ids. This is qa/gates/ledger-id-divergence.md's exact predicted failure, occurring for at least the third time, and it is no longer hypothetical: the gate should be read as demonstrated, not anticipated. NORMAL SWEEP DUTIES. One dangling handshake: qa/manifests/speaker-verbatim-token-boundary.md at ready-for-check cycle 3 with a matching Cycle checked: 3 FAIL verdict (e290653, 14:26, twelve minutes after the manifest) - the verdict